WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.100
Rule thirteen has some fine print, and the exam loves it.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:10.275
First, if you’re in any doubt whether you’re overtaking, assume that you are, and act accordingly.

3
00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:12.450
Doubt means keep clear.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.925
Second, once you’re overtaking, you stay the overtaking vessel.

5
00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:23.225
Any later change in the bearing between the two boats doesn’t turn it into a crossing situation.

6
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:25.250
So picture this.

7
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.850
You come up astern of a slow cruiser off Clearwater.

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.100
As you pull alongside, she’s on your beam, on your port side.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.525
In a crossing situation, a boat on your port side would have to keep clear of you.

10
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:41.575
Does that make you the stand-on vessel now?

11
00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.950
No.

12
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.075
You started as the overtaking vessel, and you’re still the overtaking vessel.

13
00:00:49.325 --> 00:00:52.625
You keep clear until you’re finally past and clear.

14
00:00:52.875 --> 00:00:54.750
Notice those words.

15
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.150
Getting your bow just ahead of hers isn’t enough.

16
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.525
And remember the opening phrase: overtaking overrides everything in Rules four through eighteen.
